From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the dirty-write tracker collects a guest write a 2 KiB page at a time (lost-write fix, EDEN_UP_DIRTY_PAGE_SPLIT, on by default, "0" turns it off)

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii 5e42857 (PR #1586, the "GPUDirtyMemoryManager collects a write a 2 KiB
page at a time" part) and 26bf0e1 (PR #1591, std::min<size_t> so it builds with clang), both by
Zortos (zortos293) with capy-ai; first written as 83411aa on egla146/micro. Only the
core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h page split is taken; the rest of #1586 (MayHavePending, the BACKX
verify counts, the vertex input cache, the fast-draw clock, uniform streaks, the break counter) is
not in this patch.

What: GPUDirtyMemoryManager::Collect (the list of guest CPU writes to GPU-cached memory that
GPU::InvalidateGPUCache applies) keeps one transform per 2 KiB page with one bit per 64 bytes. A
write that ran past its page end built its mask with a shift of 32 or more (undefined; on x86 and
arm64 the count wraps), so the mask came out short or empty. The part past the page, or the whole
write, was then never gathered: the buffer or texture cache keeps the older bytes (a stale buffer
or a wrong picture) until something else touches those 64-byte blocks. Our block writes
(Memory::WriteBlock and friends, HandleRasterizerWrite) hand it up to a whole 4 KiB guest page at
once, so every block write over 2 KiB, and any write that straddles a 2 KiB boundary, hits it.
Host check of the header (Mac clang -O2, scratch only): with "0", 600+1960 bytes lose all 31
blocks, 4096 bytes from a page start lose the upper 32 of 64, a 2-byte write at offset 2047 loses
both blocks; with the split nothing is lost in 8 cases.
Now Collect hands each page's part to CollectInPage (the old body). Our Collect returns whether it
stored anything (EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK / EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DOWNLOAD_LANDING fence only then):
with the split, whether any page's part stored anything.

Default ON: a pure fix. A write inside one page (nearly all) takes the loop once: a compare and a
subtraction more per collected write, and one cached switch test. A crossing write now makes one
transform per page (it may push the older one to back_buffer under the lock, as any write to a
new page does): that is the work the lost part needed all along.
EDEN_UP_DIRTY_PAGE_SPLIT=0 (exact "0"): the old single transform, for an A/B only.

---
diff --git a/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h b/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
index 34c20aac8e..fbda4e8042 100644
--- a/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
+++ b/src/core/gpu_dirty_memory_manager.h
@@ -106,14 +106,46 @@ public:
         return on;
     }
 
+    /// EDEN_UP_DIRTY_PAGE_SPLIT (zortos293/Lichii 5e42857 + 26bf0e1, #1586 + #1591, by Zortos
+    /// with capy-ai): on unless exactly "0". A transform covers one 2 KiB page with one bit per 64
+    /// bytes; Collect now hands a write that runs past its page to CollectInPage a page at a
+    /// time. "0": the old single transform, whose mask shifts by 32 or more for such a write and
+    /// can come out empty or short (the write, or its part past the page, is never gathered).
+    [[nodiscard]] static bool SplitAtPages() {
+        static const bool on = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_DIRTY_PAGE_SPLIT");
+            return !(value != nullptr && value[0] == '0' && value[1] == '\0');
+        }();
+        return on;
+    }
+
     /// Returns whether it stored anything: false when the write's bits were already collected
-    /// (EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK skips its landing check then, see Core::Memory).
+    /// (EDEN_UP_L1028_ASYNC_READBACK skips its landing check then, see Core::Memory). With the
+    /// page split: whether any page's part stored anything.
     bool Collect(PAddr address, size_t size) {
         if (BankFlagPages()) {
             // Set before the write's bytes land: a bank bind that takes the flag marks the page
             // again at the bank's next bind (BufferCache::Nx2BankFlagPages).
             CollectedWritePages().Mark(address, size);
         }
+        if (!SplitAtPages()) [[unlikely]] {
+            return CollectInPage(address, size);
+        }
+        // A write inside one page (nearly all) takes the loop once.
+        bool stored = false;
+        while (size != 0) {
+            const size_t in_page = (std::min<size_t>)(size, page_size - (address & page_mask));
+            stored = CollectInPage(address, in_page) || stored;
+            address += in_page;
+            size -= in_page;
+        }
+        return stored;
+    }
+
+private:
+    /// The old body of Collect. With the page split [address, address + size) lies in one page
+    /// and size is not 0, so the mask has bits.
+    bool CollectInPage(PAddr address, size_t size) {
         TransformAddress t = BuildTransform(address, size);
         TransformAddress tmp, original;
         do {
@@ -141,6 +173,7 @@ public:
         return true;
     }
 
+public:
     /// EDEN_UP_HELD_VS_DOWNLOAD: moves on with each Gather. A page the core reported to the GPU
     /// before must be reported again on its next write: the write held back for it has been
     /// applied. Read after Collect, it tells whether the write went into the list after a Gather.
